    <briefdescription>
<para>Identifies a unique instance of a variable. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Storage for identifying a potentially inlined instance of a variable, or a fragment thereof. This guarantees that exactly one variable instance may be identified by this class, even when that variable is a fragment of an aggregate variable and/or there is another inlined instance of the same source code variable nearby. This class does not necessarily uniquely identify that variable: it is possible that a <ref refid="classllvm_1_1_debug_variable" kindref="compound">DebugVariable</ref> with different parameters may point to the same variable instance, but not that one <ref refid="classllvm_1_1_debug_variable" kindref="compound">DebugVariable</ref> points to multiple variable instances. </para>
    </detaileddescription>
